From 64396ae3ababf19e537f07df55ec244de82dd246 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:32:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] GOLD: retire the fast-credit route and tick; pending note
 fixes from an independent review

Fast credit is removed from every entry point, not just switched off: POST
/api/gold/orders/{id}/fast-credit is an unknown route again (404 before any budget, session or
chain read), and the Worker no longer binds it, keeps the GOLD_FAST_CREDIT flag or runs the
fast-credit minute tick (Swarm audit e4a57f91 M-1, L-2..L-6 had no remaining path; L-7 is closed
by crediting only at finality). Production held one fast credit, settled, and no debt.

Independent review of 8cb7d66 (2026-10-27):
- the note took the approval hash still in wallet state while the payment was checked/sent, so
  "+N crediting" appeared before the wallet prompt and stayed after a rejected one: only a hash
  returned with phase pending/confirmed of the payment step starts it (paymentHash);
- a reverted or replaced payment now drops its note at once (paymentFailed, dropPendingCredit);
- other tabs follow note changes (storage event); the top bar checks once at once and when the
  page is shown again; the order is read from the same book as the note, not one render behind;
- deploy.mjs also re-checks gitignored .env* files after the build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
